= January 2022 — Reform without administration

Prime Minister <span class="party-pis"><b>Mateusz Morawiecki</b></span> promised that the Polish Deal would
redistribute income and prove the competence of an interventionist state. Instead, accountants,
teachers, uniformed services and small employers open January payslips they
cannot reconcile with the government's assurances. Tax offices issue one
interpretation while ministries prepare another.

At the same time, Omicron fills absences in hospitals, schools and workplaces.
Konfederacja offers one simple explanation for both crises: the state is the
problem. Lewica has to defend redistribution without defending administrative
chaos—or decide that simplicity matters more than the social purpose of the
tax system.

- @jan22_progressive
- @jan22_competence
- @jan22_workers
- @jan22_tax_revolt

@jan22_progressive
title: Defend redistribution and publish a technical repair
subtitle: Preserve the progressive principle while making PiS own the payroll failure.
on-arrival: polish_deal_stance = "Progressive defence"; labor_credibility += 4; public_trust += 1; household_policy_pressure += 2; pis_economic_position -= 2; ko_economic_position -= 1; tactical_desertion_to_ko += 0.6; barons_dissent += 2; last_policy_stage = "Advocacy"; last_policy_authority = "Parliamentary opposition"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "The Left separates progressive taxation from administrative failure"

Union accountants and Lewica policy staff publish corrected withholding tables
alongside a defence of the higher tax-free allowance and progressivity. Workers
can see which losses come from the policy and which come from a botched launch;
PiS can no longer answer every payslip with the word “reform.”

SLD officials dislike rescuing the principle behind Morawiecki's programme,
but the party retains a redistributive argument of its own.

- @jan22_resignation: The finance minister resigns


@jan22_competence
title: Join KO's indictment of governing incompetence
subtitle: Build one opposition competence case while allowing KO to define its economic content.
on-arrival: polish_deal_stance = "KO competence case"; ko_relation += 5; p2050_relation += 3; public_trust += 1; labor_credibility -= 2; ko_economic_position += 2; tactical_desertion_to_ko += 1.2; rival_relation_ko_p2050 += 1; news_headline = "The opposition makes the Polish Deal a competence scandal"

KO, Poland 2050 and Lewica assemble ministers' promises, contradictory tax
circulars and January payslips into one indictment of the government. The
case is easy to communicate and difficult for Morawiecki to dismiss.

It is also increasingly KO's case. Liberal economists move from attacking the
launch to attacking redistribution itself, while our trade-union allies ask
why Lewica supplied the witnesses and surrendered the conclusion.

- @jan22_resignation: The finance minister resigns


@jan22_workers
title: Offer a worker, pension and public-service tax floor
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: No capacity to cost the alternative.
on-arrival: polish_deal_stance = "Worker tax floor"; resources -= 1; labor_credibility += 6; household_policy_pressure += 4; workers_support += 2; pensioner_support += 2; budget_promises += 2; tactical_desertion_to_abstention += 0.5; last_policy_stage = "Proposal"; last_policy_authority = "Parliamentary opposition"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "A Left tax floor competes with both PiS and KO"

The proposal guarantees that wages, pensions and public-service salaries do
not fall during the correction, then pays for that floor with a clearer
progressive schedule. Union offices can explain it without defending the
government's software or KO's return to flatter taxation.

It is still an opposition bill and a new budget promise. The costing gives
Lewica an answer; only a parliamentary majority could make it appear on a
payslip.

- @jan22_resignation: The finance minister resigns


@jan22_tax_revolt
title: Make simplicity and lower contributions the whole answer
subtitle: Chase self-employed and professional voters by abandoning the redistributive defence.
on-arrival: polish_deal_stance = "Simplification and lower contributions"; left_economic_position += 6; left_right_score += 5; market_liberal_support += 10; liberal_professionals_left_affinity += 2; labor_dissent += 8; razem_dissent += 10; progressives_dissent += 4; konf_poll_momentum += 0.2; news_headline = "The Left enters Konfederacja's tax terrain"

Our speakers stop distinguishing design from administration and promise lower
contributions as the answer to both. Some professionals and small employers
hear a Left willing to acknowledge the burden they actually received.

Trade unionists and Razem hear the party concede Konfederacja's premise: that
the social state is chiefly an invoice. The radical right welcomes the argument
and asks voters to choose its original rather than our revision.

- @jan22_resignation: The finance minister resigns


@jan22_resignation
# prose-audit: Grade B — The resignation, the emergency patch and the administrative damage are read back through January's stance, and the capacity route is locked to having published a tax floor; the tax offices doing the corrections are still a category.
title: The finance minister resigns
subtitle: The Polish Deal's author leaves and the emergency patches begin
face-image: img/poland/events/chancellery-2022.webp
new-page: true

= January 2022 — Somebody has to have written this

Two weeks after payslips arrived smaller than anybody was told they would be,
Finance Minister **Tadeusz Kościński** resigns. Teachers, nurses and pensioners
have been under-paid because a relief threshold interacted with a contribution
rule in a way nobody modelled; the Prime Minister has ordered employers to
recalculate January retrospectively by decree, which is of doubtful legality and
is being done anyway; tax offices are answering a volume of telephone calls they
have no staff for.

The reform was not defeated in the Sejm. It passed comfortably and then failed
in the collection systems, the payroll software and the eight weeks of guidance
that were never written. That is a different kind of political failure and the
country does not yet have a vocabulary for it.

[? if polish_deal_stance = "Progressive defence": We spent January separating
the principle from the execution, which now looks less like hair-splitting and
more like the only accurate description anybody offered.?]
[? if polish_deal_stance = "KO competence case": We joined KO's competence
indictment, and KO is currently collecting the entire dividend from it.?]
[? if polish_deal_stance = "Worker tax floor": Our published tax floor is the
only opposition document that already contains the numbers a replacement would
need.?]
[? if polish_deal_stance = "Simplification and lower contributions": Having
spent January on simplification and lower contributions, we now have to explain
whether the failure was the redistribution or the plumbing.?]

- @jan22_capacity_bill
- @jan22_blame
- @jan22_compensation

@jan22_capacity_bill
title: Table the replacement schedule the ministry cannot produce
subtitle: Requires the published tax floor. Turns an opposition document into the only workable text in the room.
choose-if: polish_deal_stance = "Worker tax floor"
unavailable-subtitle: We published no costed tax floor in January — there is nothing on our shelf to put in a collapsing minister's place.
on-arrival: {!
Q.polish_deal_followup = "Replacement schedule tabled";
Q.administrative_reform_pressure =
    (Number(Q.administrative_reform_pressure) || 0) + 6;
Q.labor_credibility = (Number(Q.labor_credibility) || 0) + 6;
Q.workers_support = (Number(Q.workers_support) || 0) + 3;
Q.pensioner_support = (Number(Q.pensioner_support) || 0) + 3;
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 4;
Q.opposition_budget_credibility =
    (Number(Q.opposition_budget_credibility) || 0) + 5;
Q.media_capacity = (Number(Q.media_capacity) || 0) + 2;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left's tax schedule becomes the only finished text in the room";
!}

Our floor was costed in January because we paid for it then. It is tabled now,
with the thresholds, the transition month and the instruction sheet the
ministry never wrote, and three government deputies from committee ask for the
working file rather than the press release.

None of it passes. All of it circulates, and for the rest of the parliament the
Left is the opposition party that the finance committee's officials telephone
when they want a number checked.

- @poland_hub: Continue

@jan22_blame
title: Make the resignation the proof that the whole reform was improvised
subtitle: The obvious attack; it treats an administrative collapse as a scandal and leaves the state no better prepared for the next one.
on-arrival: {!
Q.polish_deal_followup = "Resignation as indictment";
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 2;
Q.left_poll_momentum =
    (Number(Q.left_poll_momentum) || 0) + 0.15;
Q.pis_relation = (Number(Q.pis_relation) || 0) - 6;
Q.administrative_capacity = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.administrative_capacity) || 0) - 2
);
Q.covid_anti_system_pressure =
    (Number(Q.covid_anti_system_pressure) || 0) + 3;
Q.media_capacity = (Number(Q.media_capacity) || 0) + 2;
Q.news_headline =
    "A minister's resignation becomes the whole opposition argument";
!}

He signed it, he could not run it, he has gone. Said often enough it is
effective, and it is said often enough.

It also teaches the country that a failed reform is a story about one man
rather than about a state that cannot deliver its own legislation. The tax
offices are still short-staffed in March, and nobody is arguing about that,
including us.

- @poland_hub: Continue

@jan22_compensation
title: Demand retrospective compensation for everyone underpaid in January
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Concrete, popular and it obliges us to defend a decree we have called unlawful.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The caucus cannot staff a national compensation claim.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources = (Number(Q.resources) || 0) - 1;
Q.polish_deal_followup = "Compensation demanded";
Q.household_policy_pressure =
    (Number(Q.household_policy_pressure) || 0) + 5;
Q.workers_support = (Number(Q.workers_support) || 0) + 4;
Q.pensioner_support = (Number(Q.pensioner_support) || 0) + 4;
Q.public_trust = (Number(Q.public_trust) || 0) + 3;
Q.labor_credibility = (Number(Q.labor_credibility) || 0) + 3;
Q.constitutional_restraint = Math.max(
    0, (Number(Q.constitutional_restraint) || 0) - 3
);
Q.local_network = (Number(Q.local_network) || 0) + 2;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left builds a compensation claim for January's underpaid payslips";
!}

Our regional offices open a claim desk: bring the payslip, we will tell you
what you were owed and write the letter. It is the most useful thing the party
does all winter and several thousand people who have never spoken to us walk in
with a document.

The awkwardness is on the record. The retrospective recalculation we are
enforcing rests on a decree we said the government had no power to issue, and
we are now the people making sure it is obeyed.

- @poland_hub: Continue
